unity/Udemy_Inspiration/

# Claude Code per-machine runtime cache (scheduled-task lock,
# temp transcripts) — NEVER commit. The .claude/agents and
# .claude/commands trees ARE versioned; only locks/caches are not.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/*.lock
.claude/projects/

# WorldStreamingFileRepositoryBase atomic-write sidecars. Every flush of
# `buildings_instances.json`, `item_drops.json`, lights / spawners /
# particles JSON does a tmp + File.Replace(...) with a `.bak` sidecar so
# a crash mid-write cannot truncate the previous content. The .bak is
# regenerated on every successful write — it carries no information the
# canonical .json doesn't already have, and committing it would noise
# every diff with rotating sidecar churn.
unity/Valkur/Assets/StreamingAssets/**/*.bak
unity/Valkur/Assets/StreamingAssets/**/*.bak.meta

# tools/cache/ holds intermediate JSON / report outputs from scripts under
# tools/ (e.g. music_analysis.json, unity_asset_audit.json). They are
# regenerated on demand and should never be committed.
tools/cache/

# staging/ holds raw, un-imported source art (AI-generated sheets, prop sheets,
# character sheets) waiting to go through tools/atlas/. It lives OUTSIDE
# unity/Valkur/Assets/ on purpose: anything under Assets/ is imported by Unity
# whether or not it is referenced, and these are ~250 MB of PNGs that only the
# Python pipelines read. AssetConventionsTests enforces the same boundary from
# the other side. The sheets are consumed and deleted; the manifests under
# tools/atlas/generated/ are the versioned record of what shipped.
staging/

# Downloaded CLI installer archives — local tooling, never committed.
cline-cli-*.tgz

# Cline machine-local settings (Unity editor path etc.)
.clinerules/settings.local.json

# graphify knowledge graph - derived output, rebuildable with `graphify extract . --code-only`.
# graph.json is ~66 MB and is rewritten wholesale on every build, so it is never committed.
graphify-out/
.claude/settings.json.graphify-bak
